WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
Hey, is this right, 'cause you're so busy,

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.570
you're doing so many
things, and I do wanna,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:08.690
I mean between "Brooklyn
Nine-Nine" and this terrific movie,

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.290
which I wanna talk to you about,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.850
which is, I'm gonna say this,

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.870
I love this film, I really do.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.610
And it's one of my favorite
movies that I've seen

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.040
during this whole quarantine.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.060
And I'm watching classics
like "Lawrence of Arabia"

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.937
and, you know, "Citizen Kane".

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.733
I loved everything about it.

00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:30.100
It's a great story, the
performances are incredible,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.320
and it was funny and
it was also very sweet.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.230
And then I noticed that you're

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:38.380
an executive producer in the movie,

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.500
and I thought that must be
kind of cool to be in the film,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.803
but also be executive producing
it, or is it difficult?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.580
It's a lot of work, you know,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.790
it was a small movie with a small budget,

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.780
but the pluses for me
outweigh the minuses.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.890
And a big part of that for me as an actor

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.460
is I can kind of just try stuff out

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.970
and then when I watch the
edit and feel humiliated,

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.539
I can just demand, as a producer,
that it be cut, you know?

00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:09.810
(Conan laughs)

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.350
So, it's kind of like, it's a chill vibe

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.470
for me to bring to the table (laughs).

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.001
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:15.001 --> 00:01:15.850
(Conan laughs)

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.890
But, you know, that's kind of how

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.050
I've been rolling the last few years.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.230
It's kind of, I call it
the Andre Braugher rule,

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.830
you know, where I'm a
producer on Brooklyn too,

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.480
where I'm like, just
surround me with good actors

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.810
and then we'll get in the edit.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.973
And then anytime I suck, we'll
just cut to the good actor.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.410
The cast is terrific-
They really are, yeah.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.740
In this movie.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.020
You guys all seem to work out,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.020
and then you got the incredible
J.K. Simmons to be in this.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.420
And I mean, the man's won an Oscar.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.840
Ahnd he's Jonah Jameson.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.471
And he's also Jonah Jameson
in the Spider-Man series.

00:01:50.471 --> 00:01:53.150
Yeah, I would try to get him to talk to me

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.317
as Jonah Jameson a lot and be like,

00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:59.760
"Pretend I'm Peter Parker
and be Jonah Jameson."

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.593
And he'd be like,

00:02:00.593 --> 00:02:02.475
"What, no, I'm not gonna do that."

00:02:02.475 --> 00:02:03.308
(Conan laughs)

00:02:03.308 --> 00:02:05.610
And I'd be like, "Do my outgoing voicemail

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.490
as Jonah Jameson."

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.150
And be like, "I need
pictures of Spider-Man."

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.190
(Conan laughs)

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.567
And he's like, "I'm not gonna do that.

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:14.937
"Get out of my trailer."

00:02:14.937 --> 00:02:17.354
(both laugh)

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.700
You just sound like not a
good executive producer.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.047
I was like, "Yeah, I'm
a producer,you have to!"

00:02:24.047 --> 00:02:25.476
(both laugh)

00:02:25.476 --> 00:02:26.426
Or you're fired!

00:02:26.426 --> 00:02:29.400
(both laugh)

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.573
We have a clip here.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.110
Tell us what's happening in this clip

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.470
in case anyone doesn't know.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.250
This is early on in the film and yes,

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.160
I did use the word film, thank you.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.720
It was at Sundance, big deal for me.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.820
It's early on in the film.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.653
(both laugh)

00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:45.760
You have a little gas?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.766
Did you have a little gas there?

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.030
(both clearing their throats)

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.050
Sorry, this is one of
my daughter's hair clips

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.500
just nervously picking it up.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.783
Yes, early on in the film,

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.490
and you don't yet know unless
you watched the trailer

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.230
that my character has been
reliving the same day,

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.233
many times.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.100
And I'm courting Cristin
Milioti's character, Sarah,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.180
and sort of gliding through the wedding

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.920
and doing some dancing.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.070
Let's take a look at this
clip from Palm Springs.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:16.903
Oh yeah.

00:03:18.162 --> 00:03:20.912
("Megatron Man")

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.081
And we're gonna show it.

00:04:12.081 --> 00:04:13.590
(both laugh)

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:17.420
You know what's awkward about
these interviews that we do?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.630
Is that when you come on the real show,

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.328
we then show to the clip
and it's a really good clip

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:25.130
and the audience would like
it then they would applaud

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.210
and we'd come back from it.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.000
But when we shoot this,
we add the clip later on.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.880
So, you didn't see the clip
and I didn't see the clip.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.370
We both know what the clip is.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.458
Should we...

00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:38.310
But in this moment, it's so fake.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.930
It's so fake I go "Let's take a look."

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.310
And then it's just you
and me going (sighs).

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.530
And then I go, "wow, that was great!"

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.110
But we didn't just see anything.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:46.943
We didn't see.

00:04:46.943 --> 00:04:49.300
Can we pretend like the
clip just ended again

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.580
and then you guys can put in applause

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:53.340
and we can do the like normal

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.173
thing and I will-
Yes, let's do that.

00:04:54.173 --> 00:04:55.230
I'll take a sip of my water

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.673
like it just came out of the clip.

00:04:56.673 --> 00:05:01.673
Let's take a look at this
clip from Palm Springs.

00:05:02.863 --> 00:05:05.613
("Megatron Man")

00:05:10.591 --> 00:05:11.533
(audience applauding)
We're back.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:13.553
Wow!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.863
I mean, it's a fun movie.

00:05:16.863 --> 00:05:20.100
(both laugh)

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.210
I miss that stuff.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.304
Me too!

00:05:22.304 --> 00:05:23.336
I miss those little things, when is it?

00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:24.440
I don't know.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.280
You're a smart guy and
you're behind the scenes

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.163
in the business.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.510
When do you think people
get back to acting

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.783
and making things again?

00:05:37.405 --> 00:05:38.430
That's a tough one
How's it gonna work?

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.360
How's it gonna work?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.150
I have a feeling like it can
go one of two ways, right?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.740
We will get it under control
when there's a vaccine.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.430
Or we come up with some great protocol

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:53.150
that actually feels safe
or, and hear me out,

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.450
everything goes mocap, motion capture.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.220
And we all get like
"Ready Player One" style,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.300
mocap rigs in our homes.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.040
And you can audition this way

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.270
and then actually shoot this way.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.560
It's like Avatar style, but
it's like in your real pie.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:09.010
So, you can even see in their own home,

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.940
Robert Camillo in his home
wearing a motion capture suit,

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.030
you're in your home.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.010
Yeah.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.550
And like "Ready Player
One", who with a diaper

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.690
'cause you don't wanna
waste time by leaving set.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.060
So that's also from "Ready Player One".

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.743
The book, not for all you,

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.010
posers who just like saw the movie.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.590
And they cut out the diaper
thing and pretty (mumbles).

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.020
Also the virtual sex, they cut out,

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.260
such a sellout Spielberg.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.580
Unbelievable.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.440
Anyway, but yeah, I think
if you could get like

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.330
a really good mocap rig and
like a little blue screen

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.590
or green screen room in your house.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.423
Right.

00:06:46.423 --> 00:06:49.470
With one of those 360
cameras and a diaper,

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.200
a big old diaper.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.209
Yeah.

00:06:52.209 --> 00:06:54.260
Like a big like multiple trips diaper.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.830
Wait, so you'd be using the
diaper over and over again

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:57.960
without changing it?

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.500
Yeah, so you can just shoot for days,

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.363
like in "Ready Player One", the book.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.702
Not the movie, which was a sellout?

00:07:05.702 --> 00:07:07.400
(beep) that.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.800
Okay.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.070
I did like the movie though.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.540
I did like the movie.
Yeah

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.480
That was a good move.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.280
You still got to be in the business.

